---
title: The W.E.F.T.
tags:
  - adventuring-party
date: 2025-05-12T00:00:00-04:00
campaigns: [deep-eyes]
---

The Weft is an adventuring party that has traveled across [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]], four strong at any one time, though its members changed over the years. Among them are [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]], [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]], [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] and [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]], with the [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] orbs [[People/Althane/Halidex Op-B|Hali]], [[People/Althane/Tennobrin Er-K|Tenno]] and [[People/Althane/SeRaan|SeRaan]]. They spent a favor to speak to the whole of Althane at once, announced themselves as the Weft, and called the leaders of the world to a first council at [[Geography/Althane/Athrea/Thyropae/index|Thyropae]]. The council met and opened the countries to trade and to a common defense against what lies beyond the world. They're registered with [[Org/Althane/The Guild|The Guild]] and have completed quests in the name of justice.

They keep a base at [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/index|the lava ruin]], where the Heart they woke as [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/Damien|Damien]] forges items out of divine energy. They keep their clones in coffins in an office whose owner none of them can name, with the golden needle in a drawer there. They hold the [[Phenomena/Althane/Godpiercer|godpiercer]], Divex wears the pearl [[People/Althane/Crystal Earring|Crystal Earring]], and the Weft carry a caged [[Bestiary/Mimics|tzitzimitl]]. They freed Hali and Tenno from the vats of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], and both now travel with them.

All four carry the chrome of [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]]: a skull implant, a subdermal piece, artificial lungs, and a port in the neck, cut in by [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]]'s own hand. They can see the Ret and hold credit there, and they pass for denizens of that planet. Immix named them "the Left" on a broadcast across Althane that also reached Syrin, showing a wanted-poster likeness of each of them beside a dossier of their deeds, their strength and the godpiercer. On Syrin they are known as figures of Immix's talk show, [[Divinity/Immix|the Lighthouse]], and cosplayers wear their looks.

General [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]] named them the mongrels who killed his people, broke the First House beacon and stole the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] the House kept, and their faces went out in flyers across [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] to be hunted down and hanged in the streets. They killed him at RC3, and the Deep took his body.

They killed Immix in the incomplete prison it kept, opening again the third observation of the [[Divinity/Althane/The Observers|Observers]] that Immix had taken. In the Observers' debt they are bound to hunt down and kill whoever next wrongs the pair, if they are able. From the Observers they bought a vision of the life of the Stranger, the being trapped at Althane's centre, and by it learned his true name. They killed him at the centre of Althane. The warden of [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]] once took them up to the station and gave them free run of it and its view over Althane.

They killed the Deep at the top of the City of Yellow, with aid from [[Divinity/The Narrative/Renge|Renge]]. In that fight the Deep brought the Thirteenth Realm, Althane's artificial moon, down on the city: it wiped the City of Yellow off [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]] and broke against the planet, leaving Ilkyne gone and the realm wreckage. The Weft walked out of the ruin into [[Phenomena/Althane/The Lighthouse|the Lighthouse]], rode it to a new crystal sphere it cracked open, and came back to Althane by its anchorways. The Lighthouse's central body has left the world, but its reach remains.
